# The ACPI launch's fixture driver (docs/device-matching.md "ACPI launch"):
# devmgr launches it when it admits the memory spans of an ACPI device whose
# _HID is CBIT1057, the headless gpio-launch profile's GPIO controller (no
# real device has it). Each device-memory index names an admitted span in
# _CRS order: window 1 is span 1 (the second), at most 4 MiB (the span is
# 64 KiB); window 2 is span 0 (the first), one page. "parent" is the
# controller's parent interrupt line (its first _CRS interrupt).
(Executable_Manifest
  identity => "com.cubit.test.gpio-launch-check"
  version => "0.1.0"
  drives => [(Device_Match.ACPI_ID "CBIT1057")]
  requests => [
    (device-memory "second-span" 1 4194304 Access.Read_Write)
    (device-memory "first-span" 0 4096 Access.Read)
    (platform-interrupt "parent" 0)
    (service "device-manager" "ready")
    (service "logstore" "logstore")]
  optional => ["logstore" "parent"])
